mutant: m078_hot_batch_db_seq_check_skipped
target: internal/catalog/scripts.go
failure-mode: |
  The one-round-trip inline hot batch commit (FenceBumpAt) no longer sends
  its seq check to the database. Nothing the script reads stops it, so a
  leader whose in-memory seq diverged from the catalog commits a batch that
  overlaps or skips the committed range and overwrites the seq key, on the
  path every steady-state live commit takes.
expected-detection: |
  Correct leaders never diverge, so, as for m067, the layer 3 oracle has no
  path that reaches this check. TestScripts_SeqMismatch and
  TestScripts_SeqKeyCorrupt commit an inline batch at a wrong or corrupt
  seq once the session knows its revision, and require SourceSeq
  corruption from the fallback.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

